    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0443" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.1/8736: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-21T14:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>933. From the Secretary of the Treasury for Adler.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Treasury has received reports that large scale counterfeiting of
                        Chinese currency is being practiced by the Japanese.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>If there is confirmation for these reports has this counterfeiting so far
                        had any observable consequences, and what has the Chinese Government done to
                        cope with the situation?</item>
                    <pb facs="0444" n="434" xml:id="pg434"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Any views or information you may have concerning this matter would be
                        appreciated by the Treasury Department. [Morgenthau.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
